            <div xml:id="d241">

                <pb facs="0355" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-23T13:00:00-04:00">April 23, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>615. Following is extract from Moscow’s 1246, April 18, 10 p.m., to the
                        Department<anchor n="14" xml:id="d241-f1"/> (highlights of Soviet press for
                    April 1–14, inclusive): <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Although press did not mention Ambassador Hurley’s important press
                            conference on China, significant article was published in <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Trud</hi> sharply criticizing Chinese Government
                            and Chiang Kai-shek for allegedly failing to take advantage of favorable
                            military opportunities created by Allied victories in Pacific and Burma.
                            Article was especially critical of Chungking’s alleged plans for action
                            against Communist armies. It also asserted that Chungking Government has
                            failed to honor its promises to establish political collaboration with
                            Chinese Communists.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d241-f1" n="14" xml:id="d241-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram not printed.</p>
            </note>
